An assertion reports a failure when an answer differs from its expected value. Save this complete example as score-test.mjs.

```javascript
import test from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
function clampScore(value) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(value)) return null;
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, value));
}
test('keeps scores within the limits', () => {
  assert.equal(clampScore(42), 42);
  assert.equal(clampScore(-5), 0);
  assert.equal(clampScore(125), 100);
  assert.equal(clampScore(2.5), null);
});
```

The first assertion checks an ordinary score. The next two check outside the limits. The last checks invalid input.
